course: dictionary
lesson: 8522
title: Saudi: a place and its people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Saudi is a word for things from Saudi Arabia, a large desert country in the Middle East. Look at the context: «Saudi Arabia, with its capital Riyadh, contains Mecca and Medina.» Here Saudi is part of the country's name, so it names the place.
explain: Saudi can also describe things from that country, as in a Saudi city. A Saudi, with a capital S, is a person from Saudi Arabia. In «a coalition led by Saudi Arabia», the words around it show it is the name of a country.
explain: When you meet a word like this, ask: what would fit here? Desert, Middle East and capital Riyadh are clues that tell you the place. Then swap in your meaning to check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Saudi Arabia is a large desert country in the Middle East.
fact: «Saudi» describes things from Saudi Arabia, and «a Saudi» is a person from there.
fact: Its capital is Riyadh, and the country covers most of the Arabian Peninsula.
fact: Mecca and Medina are the two holiest cities in Islam, and millions of Muslims visit them on pilgrimage, called Hajj.
fact: Saudi Arabia is very rich in oil, and it is ruled by a king.
exercise: «Saudi Arabia, with its capital Riyadh, contains Mecca and Medina.» What is the capital of Saudi Arabia? | Mecca | Yemen | *Riyadh | Medina
exercise: What is a Saudi? | A desert plant | A holy river | *A person from Saudi Arabia | A kind of oil
exercise: The text says Saudi Arabia is ruled by a king and its laws are strict. What does strict mean? | *Firm, with rules that are hard to bend | Loose and relaxed | Full of oil | Very colourful
test: «Saudi Arabia is very rich in oil.» What does rich mean here? | Old and worn | *Having a lot of oil and money | Green with plants | Poor and empty
test: Pilgrims visit Mecca and Medina on pilgrimage. What is a pilgrimage? | A kind of oil | A king's law | *A journey to a holy place | A type of desert
exam: In «a coalition led by Saudi Arabia», what job does Saudi do? | A number | A verb showing action | A colour | *Part of a country's name
